      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 50-year-old woman came to the hospital because of chest pain, mostly occurring in the early morning at rest. She performed an exercise test on Bruce protocol and exercised up to 11 min (13 METs) without chest pain. Following ergonovine provocation test, diffuse three-vessel coronary artery spasm was identified."},
